LANTERN CORE ANIMATIONS — PORTABLE IMPORT CONTRACT v1.0

FULL PNGS ARE AUTHORITATIVE
Every delivery frame is 1536x1024 RGBA, root (768,892) in top-left coordinates.
Bottom-left root: (768,132); normalized bottom-left: (0.5,0.12890625).
PNG bytes are copied unchanged. Packaging never resizes, warps, mirrors, blends,
auto-centers or changes registration. Source artwork remains untouched.

CRITICAL: KEEP THE SAME ACTOR PIXELS-PER-WORLD-UNIT
The wider canvas is transparent padding, NOT a different-sized character.
Compared with the accepted 512x640 walk, raw quad canvas dimensions become
3x width and 1.6x height at the SAME pixel scale. Padding is (+512,+320).
Do not force the padded frame into the old quad height: that shrinks the actor.
Frozen 1024x1024 R0 is unchanged; delivery adds exactly (+256,0).
No numeric runtime pixels-per-unit value is invented. Inherit the accepted walk.

TIMING AND STATES
action_role is stable: idle, attack_sword_01/02/03, dash, lantern_flare, hit, death.
clip_id and filenames may be versioned; route runtime states by action_role.
Technical fixtures have delivery_eligible=false and never enter final asset indexes.
Frames are ordered 1-based; hold_60hz is an integer number of 1/60-second ticks.
No frame blending or interpolation. Onsets and durations are derived from holds.
cycle_duration_* applies only to a looping clip; action_duration_* to one-shots.
preview_repeat_count and preview_timed_duration_seconds describe presentation
only. They never lengthen the action/cycle or turn a one-shot into a loop.
Death's finite collapse ends at D0; indefinite game-owned D0 persistence is
separate from the finite duration. Extra illustrated bridges require real slots.
R0/J1/J2 shared_state_id values must identify the exact same drawing and root.
Shared states are checked within packs and across packs with verify-shared.
Combo routing remains explicit: attack01 1-14, attack02 5-14, attack03 5-24 in the
original plan. Update routing if approved slots change; do not double-hold J1/J2.
These are assets and suggested visual events, not gameplay or collision changes.

OPTIONAL TRIMMED ATLAS
Pages are <=4096x4096. No rotation. Every allocation has 8 transparent pixels
on each side (16 between neighboring non-overlapping allocations). No extrusion.
sourceSize = full delivery canvas; sourceTrimRect = {x,y,w,h} in that canvas.
atlas_page selects atlas.pages[index]; atlasRect/atlas_rect select the crop.
All rectangle coordinates are top-left; right/bottom edges are exclusive.
To reconstruct: allocate transparent sourceSize, COPY (not alpha-composite)
atlasRect to sourceTrimRect.x,y. Use rootPivot=(768,892) on that full canvas.
Alternatively keep the trimmed image but use trimmed_root_pivot_px_top_left,
which may lie OUTSIDE the crop. Never auto-center or normalize to its bounds.
Trim includes every alpha>0 pixel without thresholding, preserving exact alpha
and visible RGB. Hidden RGB at alpha=0 outside the crop need not reconstruct;
use full PNGs when byte-for-byte original hidden RGB is required.
Empty effect frames have zero-size trim and null atlas refs; synthesize a fully
transparent full canvas. Empty actor frames are rejected by default.
Existing sampling settings are not changed. Mipmaps need separate padding-aware
validation. Alpha remains straight; do not premultiply it twice.

EXPORT WORKFLOW (Python 3.10+, existing Pillow; no new services)
1. Copy the relevant templates/<clip>.input.json and set actual final file paths.
   Paths are relative to that INPUT manifest; file may also be an absolute path.
   Preserve source_registration/native lineage fields. Templates are planning
   examples, not approval or proof of completed frames; revise counts/timing.
2. After visual QA, set artwork_approved=true. Mark exact shared state frames.
3. From the workspace root:
   python lantern_hero_core_animations_01/packaging/export_core.py export INPUT.json OUTPUT_DIRECTORY --atlas
   python lantern_hero_core_animations_01/packaging/export_core.py verify OUTPUT_DIRECTORY
   python lantern_hero_core_animations_01/packaging/export_core.py verify-shared PACK1/timing_and_registration.json PACK2/timing_and_registration.json
   python lantern_hero_core_animations_01/packaging/export_core.py zip OUTPUT_DIRECTORY ZIP_PREFIX --max-mib 30
Use a NEW output directory. Existing directories/archives are never overwritten.
Use --review-only solely for explicitly labelled unapproved fixtures.
Unknown input keys and source registration metadata are retained. Portable file
paths/derived output metadata are updated; original file paths remain source_file.
input_manifest_snapshot.json preserves the exact input data for provenance.
Source-master references are provenance, not runtime dependencies; deliver raw
masters/prompts separately in an ordinary companion ZIP if desired.

DELIVERY AND CHECKS
Target <=30 MiB per chat ZIP; --max-mib may be raised, never above 100 MiB.
Larger sets become ordinary complementary ZIPs, each independently readable.
Extract all parts into the same parent folder. No binary splits or nested ZIPs.
Each runtime package includes SHA256SUMS and validation_report.json.
Validation covers timing, source sizes, root, shared states, checksums, trim
round trips, page bounds and gutters. It does NOT certify art or engine import.
Run tests: python -m unittest discover -s lantern_hero_core_animations_01/packaging -p 'test_*.py' -v
